WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here
again to talk about language.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:10.200
And you know, I've been thinking about
a number of things and language and

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.270
people and life, and I wanna do a
series of videos where I talk about

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:20.610
sort of the human side of language,
how important language is to our being.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:25.569
And so I'm gonna talk
about language and travel.

00:00:25.569 --> 00:00:29.355
I'm gonna talk about language and
history because history is a big part

00:00:29.355 --> 00:00:30.705
of my interest in language learning.

00:00:31.365 --> 00:00:36.375
I'm going to talk about ChatGPT and the
role of the teacher in the classroom.

00:00:37.005 --> 00:00:42.105
And I'm going to talk about, uh, Elon
Musk's Neuralink, and I'm gonna do

00:00:42.105 --> 00:00:45.915
this in four separate videos, but
today I'm gonna talk about travel.

00:00:46.905 --> 00:00:49.365
One of the reasons is that
I'm going to be traveling.

00:00:49.995 --> 00:00:54.555
I'm going to be in, uh,
Denmark from the six...

00:00:54.555 --> 00:00:56.305
17th to the 19th of May.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.480
Southern Sweden, the 21st, 22nd or so.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.270
Stockholm, 24th, 25th.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:08.280
And then I'm going to be in Poland
for a week, sort of 26th, seventh

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.380
through the 2nd of June, 1st of June.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:16.000
So it would be great if we could, uh, if I
could meet some of my, uh, viewers there.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:18.930
We could talk about our
interests and our enthusiasm,

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.700
hopefully for language learning.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.540
Travel is kind of interesting
when it comes to language learning

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:28.560
because first of all, language
earning is a form of travel.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:34.320
So every time I've learned a language,
I've explored other countries.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.210
Uh, I may not be in those
countries, but I go there in a way.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.420
I get interested in the countries,
I look up the map of the

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.070
countries, I look up pictures.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.500
I get into the history of a country.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.810
Uh, it's a form of traveling.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:52.725
You're, you're traveling although
you're staying at home, you're

00:01:52.725 --> 00:01:57.554
traveling to another world, another
world in time, another world in place.

00:01:57.554 --> 00:02:01.854
So language learning is in itself
a form of travel, in my opinion.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:06.615
Second thing about travel is the idea
that you might travel to the country.

00:02:06.795 --> 00:02:09.945
Having that as a goal is
a tremendous motivator.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:16.245
Uh, now, for example, I'm gonna be in
Denmark and Poland, so I, I went and

00:02:16.245 --> 00:02:19.185
bought some audiobooks and eBooks.

00:02:19.245 --> 00:02:21.975
I'm going through a history
of Denmark right now.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.255
At some point, I'm gonna
switch over to Polish.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:29.490
Uh, I'm not gonna be fluent when I get to
Denmark or Poland, but I'll have a much

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.320
better understanding of the language.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.110
I'll be able to understand things
that are happening around me.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.730
I will try to speak.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:40.140
Um, it's gonna be
difficult, but I don't mind.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:46.140
But having this level of understanding
is gonna make it more comfortable for

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.470
me to be in the language, to be in the
country where the language is spoken.

00:02:50.025 --> 00:02:55.545
Also just listening to the audio
book and reading this book on Danish

00:02:55.545 --> 00:03:00.584
history is again, as I said, a form of
travel, uh, traveling in the language.

00:03:01.364 --> 00:03:05.505
And of course, the third thing about
travel is as many people point out,

00:03:05.565 --> 00:03:08.355
you know, if you can be in the country
where the language is spoken, that's

00:03:08.355 --> 00:03:10.334
the ultimate learning environment.

00:03:10.875 --> 00:03:15.015
Assuming that you have a good enough
level in the language so that you

00:03:15.015 --> 00:03:18.495
can take advantage, people are often
disappointed and it has happened to

00:03:18.495 --> 00:03:20.655
me, that you go to the country...

00:03:20.655 --> 00:03:23.025
I mean, I can think back to the
first time I went to Portugal.

00:03:23.175 --> 00:03:27.045
I put a fair amount of effort into
learning Portuguese and I had Spanish.

00:03:27.045 --> 00:03:30.885
And, uh, my Portuguese was not very
good, but everyone that I tried to

00:03:30.885 --> 00:03:32.475
speak to spoke to me in English.

00:03:33.105 --> 00:03:35.205
Uh, so I was unsuccessful.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:38.975
But then I went back again and
studied some more Portuguese.

00:03:39.225 --> 00:03:42.839
We, my wife and I, went to Portugal
the second time and I was able to

00:03:42.839 --> 00:03:47.399
speak to people in Portuguese, so I,
I often mention this, it's important

00:03:47.399 --> 00:03:51.959
to get your language up to a level
where it's good enough that people will

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:53.989
actually speak to you in that language.

00:03:54.029 --> 00:03:58.079
And don't get discouraged if people
answer you in English because

00:03:58.109 --> 00:04:02.040
random people in stores or on the
street, they are not your teachers.

00:04:02.399 --> 00:04:07.320
And, uh, if they feel that their
English is a more efficient way of

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:12.375
communicating then that's what they
will in many cases, use, even though

00:04:12.375 --> 00:04:16.875
you would like them to humor you in
the language that you are learning.

00:04:17.295 --> 00:04:21.405
So, but still, even if you go there,
as I did in Portuguese and I failed,

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:25.035
I was unable to really find many
opportunities to use Portuguese.

00:04:25.125 --> 00:04:28.935
And probably my Portuguese was not very
good despite the effort I had put in.

00:04:29.625 --> 00:04:33.915
Nevertheless, I came away saying,
geez, I better improve my Portuguese so

00:04:33.915 --> 00:04:35.985
that when I go again, I'll do better.

00:04:36.385 --> 00:04:42.270
So to summarize, you know, travel language
learning itself is a form of travel.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:46.560
Traveling in time and space and
language space, uh, language

00:04:46.565 --> 00:04:49.920
learning can be a goal, a motivating
goal for learning a language.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.520
You're planning to go to Mexico, you're
planning to go to China, you're planning

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.320
to go to Germany, Japan, so you're
gonna work very hard on the language.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:02.820
And third of all, when you are there,
it can be an opportunity to use the

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.740
language and to improve in the language.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:11.159
It may be difficult if your language isn't
up to the level that is needed in order

00:05:11.159 --> 00:05:14.700
for people to want to communicate with
you in the language, but then that should

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.070
be additional motivation to improve.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:21.870
So for all of those reasons, travel to
me is a big part of language learning.

00:05:22.169 --> 00:05:26.190
I've, I'm sure that many of you
have had similar experiences.

00:05:26.609 --> 00:05:27.590
Thank you for listening.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:28.429
Bye for now.

